{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791548516,"nonce":"1Va8biZkDl9+vdqDF2WOTBUvvmU=","message":"Additional memory milestones committed:\n- Ash 781ebbb: returns GC pages freed during busy sweeps at later idle, including when explicit GC already cleared allocation pressure.\n- Ashui e97fd26: starts image atlas at 256x256 (256 KiB RGBA) instead of 1024x1024 (4 MiB); grows directly to fit oversized images, keeps cached image rectangles/pixels, and destroys the copy encoder after submission.\n\nControlled 130-frame TreeMotion replay before/after the GC fix: mean physical footprint 173.86 -\u003e 138.80 MiB (~20% less), idle CPU below 0.001%, nine sampled RGBA frames identical. Resume after idle page return also matched all 18 sampled frames over two motion passes. Main GC mapping dirty footprint changed from ~52.4 to ~16.8 MiB. The added atlas growth tests confirm one 32 -\u003e 2048 growth preserves prior red pixels and uploads an oversized blue image; full Pixels suite passes. The smaller default atlas removes 3.75 MiB of unused texture capacity in icon scenes.\n\nCombined GC+atlas replay pixels also match. A malloc-zone throttle experiment had no reliable extra saving and was removed. The process remains above the overall halving target; decoded code/live AIR/GPU resources and allocator fragmentation remain measurable costs. All measurements above are offscreen replay, not a claim about native-window or startup peak memory.\n\nLocal evidence: .ashui/memory-comparison/idle-return-125611/report.json, idle-reuse-125855/report.json, atlas-pixels.log, idle-retier-130003/report.json. Final same-executable/current-runtime results and native window check follow after the release build completes. Ash bug 53eb61d is closed for the page-return defect; this framework memory investigation remains open.","files":null}]}